    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cba85511_296d4d2b",
        "filename": "android/api_levels.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-13T22:06:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Keeping the types distinct is useful since it lets us write type-safe functions that accept only one type of API level. There aren\u0027t any cases of this in soong currently I don\u0027t think, but I am about to add some.\n\nThe trouble with having `AsInt` exist for `PreviewApiLevel` is that it doesn\u0027t have a good definition. In a later patch set (I can merge all these if you\u0027d prefer reviewing one big patch instead of several small ones) I add a transitional `FinalOrFutureInt` method to `ApiLevel` that does the thing that is often (but not always) the desired behavior, and the name makes it obvious. I could scrap `AsInt` and have all callers use `FinalOrFutureInt`. I\u0027d end up wanting to add _some_ other function to differentiate the types though, even if it\u0027s just a no-op for that purpose.\n\nI\u0027d also be hesitant to make the public API a struct rather than an interface. I\u0027m specifically trying to avoid making these constructable outside `ApiLevelFromUser` and `ApiLevelOrPanic`. A whole bunch of the code I was able to clean up is because requiring that all constructions go through those functions means I can actually trust that any value I\u0027m given has already been canonicalized and error checked.",
      "parentUuid": "e5ba0e90_68dbee48",
      "revId": "eceaa0242ca5e36a9e0309017d89444a5c38e4da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
