    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9be59435_a49e3260",
        "filename": "android/api_levels.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 231,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-21T00:22:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did some digging. `sdkSpecFrom` in java/sdk.go already disallows anything other than \"current\" or an integer, and we want the codenames for other context like native and APEX where we do want to distinguish between (for example) R and S. This change should be behavior preserving in this respect, with the exception of now disallowing the use of raw numbers for non-final API levels (although 30 is an exception to this exception since it\u0027s already used in enough places, and that one is safe-ish since it\u0027s final publicly, just not in AOSP). We could clean up 30 if we wanted, but probably not worth doing.",
      "parentUuid": "23ce8778_e17d5e1f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "eceaa0242ca5e36a9e0309017d89444a5c38e4da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4ee568e_883c6619",
        "filename": "android/api_levels.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 231,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-21T01:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, there has been a request from the framework team that we shouldn\u0027t use a numbered API level before the number is determined/finalized, because 30 \u003d\u003d R, 31 \u003d\u003d S, etc. are not guaranteed until they get public. But at the same time, in the context of APEX, etc, we have a need to refer to the very next API level. We can\u0027t use \u0027current\u0027 because it points to different API levels as time goes by. So I think this change is a solution that satisfies the two seemingly conflicting needs.\n\n\u003e where \"R\" specifically means targeting a preview SDK\n\nCan we change that part? Perhaps \"R_preview\" or similar than just \"R\" might be better and less confusing.",
      "parentUuid": "9be59435_a49e3260",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "eceaa0242ca5e36a9e0309017d89444a5c38e4da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "283f6bd3_04f656ba",
        "filename": "android/api_levels.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 231,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-24T20:23:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e AFAIK, there has been a request from the framework team that we shouldn\u0027t use a numbered API level before the number is determined/finalized, because 30 \u003d\u003d R, 31 \u003d\u003d S, etc. are not guaranteed until they get public.\n\nYep, this fixes that. Before these changes there are a handful of contexts that allow non-final integers. Some of those cases were a missing check, some of them were necessary because they didn\u0027t handle codenames. After these changes, API integers are checked to ensure that they are within range, and codenames are allowed in more contexts.\n\n\u003e\u003e where \"R\" specifically means targeting a preview SDK\n\u003e\n\u003e Can we change that part? Perhaps \"R_preview\" or similar than just \"R\" might be better and less confusing.\n\nGetting this submitted will make that easier if we choose to, but I\u0027d leave that one to the people that own the Java side.\n\nRight now \"R\" isn\u0027t valid in a Java module. The case where \"R\" means \"R preview\" is the case where sdk_version is \"current\". In that case, java/android_manifest.go converts \"current\" to the codename of the current release.",
      "parentUuid": "a4ee568e_883c6619",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "eceaa0242ca5e36a9e0309017d89444a5c38e4da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
